---
layout: base.njk
title: "Changelog"
description: "The Elixir MCP tool contract changelog: what changed in each published version, which tools were added, and what breaks."
permalink: /data/changelog/index.html
canonical: /data/changelog
navActive: data
prose: true
# The Data section's tier-2 row. This page is the one static document inside an
# otherwise-app section, and it was the only one rendering without it — so
# clicking Data > Changelog dropped you out of the section's navigation
# entirely, with no way back to Dashboard or Status except the browser.
nav2Label: Data
nav2:
  - url: /data/dashboard
    label: Dashboard
  - url: /data/changelog
    label: Changelog
---
<div class="page-head">
  <h1 class="page-title">Contract changelog</h1>
  <p class="page-head__note">The MCP tool contract, version by version. Agents can read the same list through <code>elixir_changelog</code>.</p>
</div>

{%- for c in changelog %}
<section class="panel" style="margin-bottom: var(--s-4)" id="v{{ c.version }}">
  <div class="panel__head">
    <span class="panel-title mono">{{ c.version }}</span>
    <time class="mono" style="margin-left: auto; font-size: 11px; color: var(--ink-faint)" datetime="{{ c.date }}">{{ c.date }}</time>
  </div>
  <div class="panel__body">
    <p style="color: var(--ink-body); margin: 0">{{ c.summary }}</p>
    {%- if c.tools_added %}
    <p class="sample" style="margin-top: var(--s-3)">Tools added: {% for t in c.tools_added %}<code>{{ t }}</code>{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if c.breaking %}
    <p class="caveat" style="margin-top: var(--s-3)"><strong>Breaking:</strong> {{ c.breaking }}</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</section>
{%- endfor %}
